<xs:schema xmlns:xs="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema" elementFormDefault="qualified"><xs:annotation><xs:documentation>
      Operome: OperomeStGBState
      Source: StGB consolidated, offences concerning elections, public order and false testimony (provenance StGB 107, 107a, 107b, 107c, 108a, 108b, 108e, 111, 123, 125, 126a, 127, 128, 129, 129a, 130a, 138, 140, 142, 153, 157, 160; German governs)
      One combined carrier for the twenty-two sections of the final batch, spanning the Fourth chapter (election offences),
      the public-order titles, failure to report, road traffic and the Ninth chapter (false testimony). Each section is a
      SectionScope; identifiers resolve within their SectionScope. The same token (for example Publicly, InAssembly,
      Founds, Supports, RecruitsMembers, Offers, Demands) may carry a section-specific surface form: each section's
      variables are declared in that section's own groups, exactly as emitted by the per-section build, and the
      per-section schemas remain the canonical single-section substrates.
      Cross-scope by-name resolution within this carrier: the 129 scope authors the association definition
      ([Association], CRO-R80) consumed by the 129a scope per the statutory reference to Section 129(2); the 157 scope
      authors the testimony-in-distress exception ([TestimonyInDistress], TID-R80, the inserted-ausser transformation)
      consumed as a negative leg by the 153 scope (FUT-R80). The 127 scope authors the trading-platform definition
      ([TradingPlatform], CTP-R80) consumed locally; the 108e scope authors the live unjustified-advantage exemption
      ([AdvantageNotUnjustified], BER-R80) consumed locally.
      Struck catalogues resolve as inputs: the 127 qualifying-offence list, the 129 two-year severity threshold, the
      138 eight-number offence catalogue and the 140 reference list are struck in the source; catalogue membership
      stands as an input variable in each scope. The 129a directed-at catalogues mix in-corpus references with
      out-of-corpus statutes (VStGB, KrWaffKG, WaffG and paragraph ranges beyond the encoded scopes) and resolve
      partially, the Section 310 pattern; its paragraph 5 reference to the struck paragraph 3 likewise resolves as input.
      Intent and knowledge elements retained per the retention criterion: 107b legs 2 and 3 (knowledge), 107c
      (knowledge intention), 125 (readiness purpose), 126a (manner intended), 130a (readiness determination and purpose).
      Objective Tatbestand only; sanctions, grading, attempt, procedure and sentencing discretion excluded; silent
      repairs against the German recorded in the Flags annexes of the working document, not here.
      Runtime caveat: this carrier is a consolidated file, not a proven executable, until the runtime loader's
      scope-local resolution is tested once against the evaluator.
    </xs:documentation><xs:appinfo><PackageMeta><Subject>StGB Consolidated, Elections, Public Order and False Testimony (§107 to §160)</Subject><Verb>commit</Verb><Article>StGB 107, 107a, 107b, 107c, 108a, 108b, 108e, 111, 123, 125, 126a, 127, 128, 129, 129a, 130a, 138, 140, 142, 153, 157, 160</Article><ShortName>OperomeStGBState</ShortName></PackageMeta></xs:appinfo></xs:annotation><xs:simpleType name="TristateEnum"><xs:restriction base="xs:string"><xs:enumeration value="true"/><xs:enumeration value="false"/><xs:enumeration value="unknown"/></xs:restriction></xs:simpleType>

